{
    "background_story": "Makai was a young and talented artist from Tokyo, who had always been fascinated by the masterpieces of the Louvre Museum in Paris. As a child, he spent hours poring over books and documentaries about the museum's vast collection. After completing art school, Makai won a prestigious scholarship to study at the \u00c9cole des Beaux-Arts in Paris. He spent countless hours sketching and painting in front of the Louvre's iconic works, including the Mona Lisa. Inspired by the museum's rich history and artistic treasures, Makai's own style began to flourish. His artwork, a fusion of traditional Japanese techniques and French Impressionism, soon gained international recognition. The Louvre, which had once been a distant dream, became a second home to Makai, who went on to exhibit his own work within its hallowed halls.",
